v 3
d writeinput: turn the data in memory into a self-contained, reproducible input command block
d
d writeinput converts the data in memory, or a filtered subset of it, into an
d input command a reader can paste to reconstruct the dataset exactly - the
d standard way to post a minimum working example on Statalist or Stack Overflow.
d It is built for bit-for-bit fidelity: precision(hex) writes doubles as %21x so
d nothing is lost in the round trip, extended missing values (.a through .z) are
d detected and preserved, and every string is wrapped in compound double quotes
d so internal quotes and backticks cannot break the block.  Works with frames,
d if/in, and random sample drawing; variable labels can be emitted as comments
d and value labels decoded into the example.  Output goes to a .do file, to the
d results window (dryrun), or as a fenced code block for GitHub (markdown).
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth, Sr Researcher, Texas 2036
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
f writeinput.ado
f writeinput.sthlp
